From 2aaa4107b994c83a0e14341d53d1f6f2d326b0a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:54:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: a change of mode on a dual-mode connector of
 nvidia-drm turns the output off and on

Through the HDMI port of the HP ZBook 17 G6, a dual-mode DisplayPort connector that nvidia-drm
drives as HDMI (DP-2, issue #4), a change of the refresh rate made on a running head did not reach
the TV: with 1.0 RC3, a video at 23.976 Hz played with the TV still at 60 Hz, while the DRM state
had the mode of 24 Hz; through a USB-C to HDMI adapter of the same laptop (DP-1) the change of rate
worked; and with 1.0 RC4, whose exit from native Dolby Vision turns the head off and on in the
mode of the video, the rate was taken at least sometimes, never before it. On that connector
native Dolby Vision already enters and leaves with the head turned off and on, so that NVKMS
brings the head and the link up from scratch; every change of mode there now goes out so too:

 - CWinSystemGbm::SetFullScreen(): the new mode is committed with the head off, with the frame of
   the change of mode, and then the head is turned on again (FlipModeFromScratch());
 - the change of mode for an HDR video is not held for its HDR signalling there
   (CModeChangeHold::StartHolds(): Change::modeFromScratch): the mode goes out alone first, from
   scratch, and the signalling with the next commit, as the transport of native Dolby Vision does;
 - native Dolby Vision that ends is restored with the mode that Kodi sets next in one bring-up of
   the head in that mode (FlipDVBridgePage()), not in place.

Only where NVIDIA_DUAL_MODE::ModeChangeRestarts() says: a DisplayPort connector whose
NV_DUAL_MODE_TMDS is 1 now (the card drives the display as HDMI itself), the output meant to be
on, another mode. An HDMI connector, a DisplayPort display, the panel of a laptop and every
connector of the kernel backends change nothing (the RTX 4080 SUPER and the LG C5 among them).

Fail closed: a refusal of the commit with the head off falls back to the request before it, and
the commit after it makes the change in place, as before ("Turning the output off for the change
of mode ... was refused ...: the mode went out in place, as before"); where the head cannot be
turned on again, it is asked to again with the frames after it, after 1 s and then less often, as
after a flip that did not come (FlipOutputOn()). kodi.log says each change made so ("The change of
mode to WxH @ R Hz went out with the output turned off and on again on connector DP-2 ...").
<video><dualmoderestart>false</dualmoderestart></video> in advancedsettings.xml makes the changes
of mode in place there, as before.

The host test of the entry (dpdual_test) covers it: on DP-2 the change to 23.976 Hz is no change on
a running head, the head is brought up with it; with the setting off, in place; HDMI-A never; the
hold of HDR on HDMI as before. The decisions of 1.0 RC4's dualmode_test (1537 combinations without
the new field) are the same. Whether the TV takes the rate this way can only be seen on that
laptop: not verified.
